import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'..')
from con_helpers import *
save(5,5,"The Technology of Knowledge, Solitude, and Community","Take one belief about yourself that stings. Is it a wave passing through awareness, or a wave you have glued an identity to?",[
mc("U","What makes the fourth doorway, knowledge, different from the first three, according to Conversation 5.5?",
 ["It goes after the one assumption that the mind’s contents are you, not just the surface marks.","It asks for more hours of practice than the first three, and a quieter place to do them in.","It replaces the other doorways, which can be left behind once the knowing has been grasped.","It works only on thoughts, whereas the first three work only on the body and the breath."],0,
 "Rhythm, attention and action each lighten what gets laid down in the mind. Knowledge goes for the single unnoticed assumption underneath: that the thoughts, moods and habits are who you are. It is not more reading or harder thinking, but one act of seeing, repeated.",
 "Knowledge cuts at the root assumption that the mind’s contents are you","Part 1"),
mc("A","A man tells himself, “I am an anxious person,” and feels that it is a life sentence. Which move fits Conversation 5.5?",
 ["Agree that it is his nature, and learn to live inside the limits that nature sets.","See the anxiety as a wave passing through the awareness he is, and loosen the identification.","Push the anxiety away at once, since feeling it only makes the identification stronger.","Argue himself out of the anxiety by listing every reason that he has to feel safe."],1,
 "I am anxious is a life sentence; anxiety is a wave passing through awareness is weather. The fact does not change, but the identification, which was the prison, does. Each genuine seeing of a wave as a wave un-glues one identification.",
 "See the feeling as a passing wave, and the identification loosens","Part 1"),
mc("U","What is the relationship between viveka (clear seeing) and vairāgya (loosening the grip), according to Conversation 5.5?",
 ["They are rival paths, and each person should follow just the one that suits.","Vairāgya is the harder of the two, and viveka is only a preparation for it.","They are twins: either alone fails, and together the craving deflates.","Viveka is for the head, and vairāgya is for the heart, so they never meet in one act."],2,
 "Seeing without loosening is merely clever; loosening without seeing is dry suppression, which strengthens what it fights. Together, you see that what you chased was passing and that the chase came from feeling incomplete, and the craving deflates, not crushed but seen through.",
 "Seeing and letting go are twins; together a craving deflates","Part 1"),
mc("A","Someone has a flash of insight at a talk, but by evening ordinary life has shut the door on it. Which view fits Conversation 5.5?",
 ["The insight was false, since a true recognition would not fade with the evening news.","She should give up, since the flash shows that realisation is not for ordinary people.","She should wait for another flash, and in the meantime put the matter aside.","The mind still holds contrary assumptions, and digesting examines each one until it loosens."],3,
 "The second stage, digesting, is the patient work of taking each assumption, such as I am this body or I am my memories, and examining it honestly. Nothing is asked to be swallowed; everything is examined. That is what lets the recognition take hold.",
 "Digesting examines each contrary assumption until it loosens","Part 2"),
judge("“Hearing the teaching is a one-time event, and a single great statement, once heard, completes the path of knowledge.”",F,
 "Hearing is sustained, attentive reception over months and years, laying down lightening marks that accumulate quietly. A great statement lands when long hearing has prepared the ground, and the recognition fades again. Digesting and then living it follow. The flash is not a magic spell.",
 "Hearing accumulates over years; one great statement does not finish the path","Part 2"),
mc("A","A man asks how to test whether good company actually helps his practice, being sceptical of any claim of transmission. What does Conversation 5.5 suggest?",
 ["Take the claim on trust at first, since doubt will block whatever the company can give.","Sit in good company and observe whether his own practice deepens between meetings.","Judge the people by their words, and join whichever group argues most convincingly.","Avoid company altogether, since a sceptic does best working entirely on his own."],1,
 "Swamiji keeps the scepticism and asks only for a test. A calm person steadies a tense room, and some company lightens us while other company heavies us; the effect has a top end. No belief is needed in advance: observe, and report good or null.",
 "Test company by watching whether the practice deepens between meetings","Part 3"),
mc("A","A friend has stopped answering calls and seldom leaves the house, and says she is just taking solitude. Which question fits Conversation 5.5?",
 ["Can she engage with people, and is she choosing to step back, or can she not engage at all?","Is she meditating each day, since solitude is only real when it includes a practice?","Is she happy, since solitude that brings happiness is always the healthy kind?","How long has it lasted, since only a very long solitude can be called a retreat?"],0,
 "Healthy solitude is an engaged person stepping back on purpose to do inner work, intending to return. Withdrawal from collapse is a person who cannot engage at all. From outside they look the same; inside, one is recalibration and the other is shutdown, which needs help first.",
 "Chosen solitude differs from collapse: can she engage, and is it her choice","Part 3"),
judge("“Solitude turns the incoming signal down, so the mind can hear its own patterns, and the company of the true turns the input toward a higher source.”",T,
 "Solitude is a precise instrument: the deliberate turning down of the flood of input so that clear seeing has room to work. Satsaṅga, the company of the true, is the mirror image, turning the input toward the best source, so that a community pulls each member higher than any could climb alone.",
 "Solitude turns the input down; good company turns it toward a higher source","Part 3"),
mc("A","A man in a heavy, foggy state wants to begin at once with the inquiry into who he really is. What does Conversation 5.5 advise?",
 ["Begin at once, since a mind in fog is the one that most needs clear seeing.","Give it up for good, since this doorway is meant for only a few special people.","Go back to rhythm first, so that the inquiry does not dissolve into mist.","Wait for the fog to lift of itself, and take no step at all in the meantime."],2,
 "This doorway needs a mind steady enough to hold the seeing. In the heavy drift, the discrimination dissolves into mist, so rhythm comes first; in the fast drift the reflection scatters, so attention training comes first. It is the plain order of things, and each step is worth doing for its own sake.",
 "Heavy drift: rhythm first, so the inquiry has an instrument to work with","Part 3"),
judge("“The four doorways are four equal alternatives, and a person can start with whichever one sounds most appealing.”",P,
 "Each doorway is worth doing for its own sake, and any of them can serve a person fully. But they also build: rhythm steadies the body, attention steadies the mind, action cleans the daily stream, and then knowledge has a clear enough instrument. The knowledge doorway in particular needs the others first.",
 "The doorways are each worthwhile, yet they build one on another","Part 3")])
